.* Caribbean Stud Poker Help
:userdoc.

:h1 res=001.General Help
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
Caribbean Stud Poker is a popular casino game&colon. you play five card stud against the dealer, Sarah. It is fast, lets you decide whether to continue, and allows the most reckless wagers. Choose a topic&colon.
:p.
:ul compact.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=002.How to begin:elink.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=003.Rules of the game:elink.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=004.Progressive jackpot:elink.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=005.Statistics:elink.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=006.Payout table:elink.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=007.Strategy:elink.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=008.Menus and keys:elink.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=009.About Caribbean Stud Poker and license:elink.
:eul.
:p.


:h1 res=002.How to begin
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
Just like the real thing, you need money to play. Choose :hp2.Game - Add $100:ehp2. (or press :hp2.Add $100:ehp2.) to add money to the bank. When you finish, choose :hp2.Cash Out:ehp2. to take your chips home.
:p.
Adding and cashing out simulate buying and cashing in chips. All money activity is recorded in the :link reftype=hd res=5.statistics:elink. window, so you can follow how much you have lost.
:p.
When the bank holds three times the ante (set in the spin field next to the :hp2.Ante:ehp2. button), you can ante. Press :hp2.Ante:ehp2. to start a hand. To play for the :link reftype=hd res=4.progressive jackpot:elink., press :hp2.Progressive:ehp2. to wager $1. The :hp2.Auto:ehp2. box plays the progressive on every hand.
:p.
Once the hand is dealt you decide to :hp2.Bet:ehp2. or :hp2.Fold:ehp2.. If you are unsure, the :hp2.Advice:ehp2. button suggests a play.

:h1 res=003.Rules of the game
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
You play alone against the dealer, :hp2.Sarah:ehp2.. A hand starts when you place the ante in the :hp2.ante:ehp2. field. You may also wager $1 for the progressive jackpot.
:p.
Sarah deals five cards to you and five to herself, one of which is face up. You can then fold, giving up the ante, or bet.
:p.
If you bet, an amount equal to twice the ante goes into the :hp2.bet:ehp2. field. Sarah then turns over her other four cards.
:p.
The dealer must hold at least Ace/King to qualify. If she does not qualify, you get back the ante and the bet, plus a payment equal to the ante.
:p.
If the dealer qualifies, her hand is compared with yours. If yours is higher, you are paid the ante and bet back, a payment equal to the ante, and the bet multiplied by the payout of your hand (see :link reftype=hd res=6.Payout table:elink.). If the dealer's hand is higher, she takes the ante and the bet. A tie returns ante and bet.

:h1 res=004.Progressive jackpot
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
On any hand you may wager $1 for the progressive jackpot. Hands from a flush up pay from the jackpot, either a fixed sum or a percentage of it, as long as you bet (the jackpot is paid even if the dealer's hand wins).
:p.
In a real casino the jackpot grows with the number of players. In this single player game it grows continuously.
:p.
:link reftype=hd res=006.Payout table:elink.

:h1 res=005.Statistics
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
To help you decide on a strategy the game records statistics. Choose :hp2.Game - Statistics:ehp2. (or press :hp2.Stats:ehp2.) to see how many hands of each kind were dealt, your wins and losses, the money added and cashed out, and the progressive payouts. :hp2.Reset:ehp2. clears them.

:h1 res=006.Payout table
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
If you bet and win, you receive the ante and bet back, an additional ante, and a multiple of the bet as shown below. The progressive column applies if you played the progressive.
:p.
:dl tsize=22 break=all.
:dt.:hp2.Royal Flush:ehp2.
:dd.Payout&colon. 100&colon.1   Progressive&colon. 100%
:dt.:hp2.Straight Flush:ehp2.
:dd.Payout&colon. 50&colon.1   Progressive&colon. 10%
:dt.:hp2.Four of a Kind:ehp2.
:dd.Payout&colon. 20&colon.1   Progressive&colon. $500
:dt.:hp2.Full House:ehp2.
:dd.Payout&colon. 7&colon.1   Progressive&colon. $100
:dt.:hp2.Flush:ehp2.
:dd.Payout&colon. 5&colon.1   Progressive&colon. $50
:dt.:hp2.Straight:ehp2.
:dd.Payout&colon. 4&colon.1
:dt.:hp2.Three of a Kind:ehp2.
:dd.Payout&colon. 3&colon.1
:dt.:hp2.Two Pair:ehp2.
:dd.Payout&colon. 2&colon.1
:dt.:hp2.Pair:ehp2.
:dd.Payout&colon. 1&colon.1
:dt.:hp2.Ace/King:ehp2.
:dd.Payout&colon. 1&colon.1
:edl.

:h1 res=007.Strategy
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
With a house advantage of almost 4 percent the best strategy is not to play. If you do play, consider&colon.
:ul.
:li.With :hp2.nothing:ehp2., fold. The dealer qualifies more often than not.
:li.With :hp2.Ace/King:ehp2.&colon. bet if the dealer shows two through queen and you hold a card of the dealer's face up card; bet if the dealer shows an ace or king and you hold at least a jack; otherwise fold.
:li.With a pair of twos, threes or fours&colon. bet if your pair is higher than the dealer's face up card, if the dealer's card is an ace or a king, or if you hold a card of the dealer's face up card; otherwise fold.
:li.Always :hp2.bet:ehp2. with a pair of fives or better.
:eul.

:h1 res=008.Menus and keys
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
The following keys are assigned&colon.
:dl tsize=10.
:dt.:hp2.A:ehp2.
:dd.Ante
:dt.:hp2.B:ehp2.
:dd.Bet
:dt.:hp2.F:ehp2.
:dd.Fold
:dt.:hp2.V:ehp2.
:dd.Advice
:dt.:hp2.S:ehp2.
:dd.Statistics
:dt.:hp2.F1:ehp2.
:dd.Help
:dt.:hp2.Ctrl+N:ehp2.
:dd.New Game&colon. clears the table and sets the bank to $100
:dt.:hp2.Ctrl+X:ehp2.
:dd.Exit
:dt.:hp2.Ctrl+F:ehp2.
:dd.Frame Controls&colon. hides or shows the title bar and menu
:edl.
:p.
Options - Sound switches the sound effects on or off. Options - Language selects English, Spanish, Dutch, German, French or Italian; menus, dialogs and this help change at once. Options - Save settings on exit stores the settings, bank, jackpot and statistics in CStud.cfg.

:h1 res=009.About Caribbean Stud Poker and license
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
Caribbean Stud Poker is part of The Compulsive Gambler's Toolkit by IglooSoft (1999), released as open source in 2002. The Open Watcom version was prepared by the OS2World community in 2026.
:p.
Caribbean Stud Poker is free software&colon. you can redistribute it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by the Free Software Foundation, either version 3 of the License or (at your option) any later version. It is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY. See the file LICENSE.txt.

:euserdoc.
